 Responsibilities: 
 • Process Engineer is in charge to support APU on process reliability and improvement activities to have efficient
machines and standard equipment.
- Maintain equipment reliability and performance
- Continuous improvement and productivity
- Safety improvement
- Support industrialization of new products 

 Maintain equipment reliability: 
 • Understand product / process specifications and customer requirements;  

• Define standard equipment documentation to use equipment properly; 

• Define process flow chart and write standard instructions; 

• Define maintenance level 1, Work Instructions and technical documentation;  

• Train operators / set-up technicians to standard process and Work Instructions; 

• Support machine performance targets and TRP improvement; 

• Provide technical support to APUs on day to day problem solving and analysis. 

 Continuous Improvement and productivity: 
 • Define cycle time improvement plan and contribute to -30 Plan savings; 

• Lead cycle time reduction workshops; 

• Detect muda on process and define action plan to improve machine efficiency; 

• Support productivity workshop deployment in APUs; 

• Support TPM methodology (ERIM program) and support training deployment; 

• Support VPS workshop (HOSHIN, 5S, SMED, change over…); 

• Lead process modification meeting with APU managers, understand production needs, define planning and select suppliers to achieve SQCD targets; 

• Be involved in packaging validation and internal flow improvement; 

•  Propose technical Improvements; 

• Join VPS Committee on request;

• Review / Improve Process FMEA to reduce risks and make sure action plan is implemented (update PFMEA after APU QRQC);

 Safety improvement: 
 • Is responsible to eradicate ergonomic and safety issues when detected; 

• Join ergonomy and safety assessment for any new equipment, machines or relayout; 

• Perform regular audits on process to make sure operators are running equipment properly with no ergonomic and safety issues; 

• To apply the SPV rules  

• Escalate to APU Mgrs if any deviation to standard (WI, PPE…); 

• Others: Save nature resources, energy and paper &amp; Obey the EHS laws and related
requirements, implement the EHS regulations, procedures and work instructions. 

 Industrialization of new products: 
 • Support new product industrialization and modifications (ensure respect of IProM); 

• Interface with projects and Production to prepare new equipment, meet performance and  cost targets; 

• Respect and ensure respect of safety and VPS rules for new process development; 

• Manage the process development documentation, WI and support operator training;

• Take part in pre-serial trials and FDPR (Full Day Production Runs) to confirm that the
process is robust enough to go into mass production (Process PY check, OK-Start procedure,
Cpk).

• Work with Process PTM to approve standard conditions and SOP;

• Propose technical solutions to improve machine performance and have efficient new product
industrialization;

• Support out-sourcing and re-insourcing activities in APUs (if any).

